there is a growing mystery surrounding  the disappearance of a Saudi journalist  who's been critical of Saudi Arabia's  powerful crown prince Washington Post  contributor Jamal Khashoggi vanished in  Turkey last week after entering the  Saudi consulate he'd been living in  self-imposed exile in the United States  the State Department says it is closely  following his disappearance in Istanbul  Holly Williams is outside the Saudi  consulate there Holly good morning good  morning this is a bizarre and disturbing  story Jamal has Shoji a respected Saudi  Arabian journalist visited the Saudi  consulate here in Istanbul Turkey last  Tuesday  apparently in order to get an official  document that he needed to marry his  Turkish fiancee but after entering the  building which you can see just behind  me he disappeared and his fiance and  friends say they haven't heard from him  since Turkish officials have told  journalists they believe her soldier was  murdered inside the consulate but so far  they've provided no evidence to back  that claim up Saudi Arabia denies that  it murdered or abducted her Shoji and  officials even allow journalists inside  the consulate in an attempt to prove  that he is not there now Jamal has  showed he had spoken out against the  Saudi government in its powerful Crown  Prince Mohammed bin Salman condemning a  lack of free speech in the  ultra-conservative Islamic state under  the Crown Prince Saudi Arabia has  launched a series of social reforms  including allowing women to drive but at  the same time the Saudi government has  become increasingly intolerant of any  form of dissent locking up critics and  rights campaigners Gayle Thank You Holly  Williams reporting from Istanbul
 

